cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these codes or data, please cite the article given as the preferred citation."
title: "Noncommutative Schwarzschild black holes at second order: codes and data"
abstract: >-
  Codes and data of the article "Noncommutative Schwarzschild black holes at second order:
  the correct metric, a branch cut at the horizon, and the quasinormal spectrum by eight
  methods". The exact computations derive the tetrad and the metric of the Schwarzschild
  black hole deformed at second order in the noncommutativity parameter by the
  Seiberg–Witten map, compare the two published versions with them, and check the radial
  equation, its angular sums and the values of its potential at the horizon. The numerical
  codes compute the scalar quasinormal spectrum, the eigenvalues of a nonlinear problem with
  a branch cut, by eight methods: spectral collocation solved by a Joukowski map, by the
  fully rational Krylov method NLEIGS in two realisations, by contour integrals and by
  Newton's method in high precision, a Jost function, exterior complex scaling, time
  evolution, and high-order WKB with Padé approximants. The data are those of every table
  and figure of the article.
